# .cursorrules
# Project-level context. Skills handle workflow logic — keep this lean.

## Critical rule

Before touching ANY UI file, read `design.md` in full.
It is the source of truth for all visual decisions on this project.

## Skills available

Three skills are installed in `.cursor/skills/`:

- **extractor** — reads design source, populates design.md. Run first on any new project or after design changes.
- **builder** — implements UI from design.md. Includes full-cycle-dev phases (Figma→code, review, QA).
- **qa** — reviews output against design.md. Always produces a report.

Sequence: extractor → builder → qa. Never skip.

## When design changes

1. Update `## Active Design Decisions` in design.md first
2. Run extractor skill if Figma/screenshots changed
3. Run builder skill on affected sections
4. Run qa skill before considering done

## Hard rules (always on)

- No colors outside design.md tokens
- No generic Tailwind blue as primary
- No Lorem Ipsum
- No unsolicited animations or effects
- Flag every judgment call explicitly
